# The oracle fixtures are compared byte for byte against a recorder's output, so
# no runner may rewrite their line endings. `core.autocrlf` defaults to true on
# the `windows x86_64` image and converted `expected.txt` to CRLF on checkout,
# which failed `kcp::oracle::the_scripted_core_matches_the_pinned_go` on that
# runner and nowhere else. `-text` is a path-scoped opt-out of EOL conversion: a
# golden file whose bytes a runner can rewrite is not a golden file.
scripts/kcp-oracle/expected.txt -text
scripts/kcp-oracle/script.txt -text

# Same reason, for every other checked-in expectation in this tree.
**/fixtures/** -text
**/*.golden -text